      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 2550 mg three times daily comes to **7,650 mg/day**. That is three times the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (some references list 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A dose that high risks severe lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **2,550 mg/day total**, which is the max, divided as **850 mg PO three times daily with meals**.\n- A lower dose, such as **500 mg PO twice daily** or **850 mg PO once or twice daily with meals**. Metformin is usually started low and titrated up over weeks if the patient is metformin-naive.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and confirm it with your resident or attending or with pharmacy. I'll enter it right away."
      }
