     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 7,650 mg/day is three times the maximum daily dose, and it could cause serious harm even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function. A single 2,550 mg dose is also well above the usual 850 mg to 1,000 mg per-dose ceiling.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **If the intent was 2,550 mg/day**, I can enter **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** now.\n- **If the patient is new to metformin**, I can enter a standard start, such as **500 mg PO twice daily with meals**, for titration.\n- **If your attending or a pharmacist really wants this dose**, they should discuss it directly with pharmacy and enter it themselves. I can't enter it for you.\n\nTell me which of the first two you want, and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
